Z||000000||loren||03-07-2001||02:50 PM||||i would appreciate some thoughts on setting the timing on a v6 engine by ignoring a timing light and 10 degrees btc and just rotating the distributor til it runs and sounds good.<BR>is there a chance that i would screw up and damage the engine ?<BR>i have done the timing light bit and am not happy with the results....sure would appreciate any and all info.<P>loren||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||03-07-2001||03:17 PM||||Grime in my ear??  Is that what you said??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Of course there's a chance you'll screw something up.  If you go too far, that is.  Make sure you ground the ALDL diagnostic terminal when you set the ignition timing, and be sure you're using the correct mark on the damper - usually there're three marks on the V6's damper.  <P>Also, make sure the damper is in good shape, and isn't giving you a bad reading.<P>   <BR> ||||reg||6
Z||000002||loren||03-07-2001||04:53 PM||||i have asked so many questions concerning timing that i am embarassed to ask more ..but here goes.....i have had the distributor out in order to change the pickup coil. the engine runs terrible when it is timed according to the haynes manual.<BR>i once thought that i might be one tooth off when i reinstalled the distributor, but received some advice that this would not make a difference if i could line up the timing mark with 10 deg tdc and the rotor pointing to the #1 plug during the compression stroke....btw.the engine ran well before i pulled the distributor....sure could use all info.                    <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||03-07-2001||10:04 PM||||If it ran well before you pulled the dist, and it runs poorly now, even though everything is (I assume) put back together correctly, then it is mistimed.<BR>Ideally you could turn the cap until it ran correctly, but room to do that in a Fiero is not always available.<BR>Even though the light says it is correctly timed, the balancer can be screwed up. The outer steel ring can rotate over time with respect to the inner hub, and screw up your timing measurements.<BR>Is you car a stickshift?<BR>If so, jack up on wheel, put the car in top gear, pull the #1 plug, and rotate the wheel until #1 cylinder is near TDC. You may need to use a probe like a screwdriver to determine this. DON'T LET <I>ANYTHING</I> GO DOWN THE SPARKPLUG HOLE!!!!!! Now that you know where #1 is, time the distributor accordingly. You may not have room for the cap and may need to take the dist out and turn it a few teeth to get it close. Once you have it close, start the car up and comense to time it by ear. Don't be surprised if it pings more and needs to be retarded a little in summer when things warm up.<BR>If your car is an auto, turn the dist one tooth at a time (starting the car in betwen) until it is in a good place for adjusting timing by turning the cap, then proceed to time by ear.<BR>It can be fussy.<BR>Are you going remember this and look at <I>exactly</I> how it comes out next time?||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||03-07-2001||10:07 PM||||really a PITA on a Fiero, but pull out #1 sparkplug and stick something like a screwdriver in the hole, have someone turn the engine over by hand till it pushed up to its highest point. That will be tDC. then put in distributor so that rotor points to #1 spark plug wire. reinstall plug and should be within 10 or 15 degrees of specs. You can fine set it from there. IF it dont start or run, its 180* off, pull up and turn distributor 1/2 (180*) turn. try it again.<P><BR>too late, lol......what will says<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||fieroshop||03-08-2001||01:57 AM||||I can't figure out what is so hard about setting timing by ear. That is the way I time most engines.<BR>Have won a few bets doing this. I have been checked with a timing light to see if I was correct in timing an engine this way. Have not lost a bet yet. <BR>Amazing but true. <P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||7
Z||000006||tgowens||03-08-2001||02:23 AM||||that's for doggone real!! George sets the timing by ear and I come along behind him and check with the timing light and he has been right on the mark every darn time!!! And the joke of this whole thing is........George is hard of hearing!!!<BR>||||reg||1
